# Raphael backend secrets.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the directory you run `raphael` from - loading follows the invocation
# directory, not the installed package - or set the variable in your environment directly. A variable
# already set in the environment always wins over this file, including when it is set to an empty
# value, which then fails startup rather than silently falling back here.
#
# This file is an example and is committed. `.env` is ignored and must never be committed.

# The single full-access API key for this instance. Required: the server will not start without it.
#
# Generate a random one:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# At least 32 characters, and visible ASCII only - no spaces, control characters, or accented or
# non-Latin characters. That last restriction is not cosmetic: HTTP headers carry bytes, so a key with
# a non-ASCII character would let the server start and then fail every client, and most HTTP clients
# refuse to send one at all. Raphael rejects such a key at startup rather than reporting a
# configuration that cannot work.
#
# Length is not strength - 32 repeated characters would pass and still be a weak key - so generate it
# rather than inventing one. Hex or base64url is recommended: both stay inside the accepted alphabet
# and avoid the `#` character, which a `.env` parser treats as the start of a comment in an unquoted
# value and would silently truncate. Quote the value if it contains anything unusual. Whitespace is
# rejected rather than trimmed, because a credential is used exactly as written or not at all.
#
# Every client - mobile, web, CLI, agent - uses this one key. Rotating it means updating all of them.
RAPHAEL_API_KEY=
